+sources and supporting evidence.}{MCTS offers a way to gather evidence incrementally by allocating successive rollouts to promising states \citep{silver2016mastering,kocsis2006bandit,browne2012survey}. In a cyclic graph, ordinary tree search indexes states by walk prefixes, so repeated visits create multiple copies of the same physical record \citep{childs2008transpositions,kishimoto2004general,saffidine2012ucd,moerland2020mcts}. These copies consume rollout budget and spread value estimates across repeated instances of the same record. Prior Monte Carlo graph search shares transpositions in acyclic search graphs \citep{czech2021monte}, while feedback-edge methods obtain directed acyclic graph (DAG) approximations by removing or reorienting edges \citep{eades1993fast,berger1990approximation}. Risk extraction requires a search representation that preserves cyclic relations while consolidating evidence about the same physical records.}
